{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/unicode-org/icu4x/pulls/8143","id":3940972360,"node_id":"PR_kwDODoHqRc7q5ndI","html_url":"https://github.com/unicode-org/icu4x/pull/8143","diff_url":"https://github.com/unicode-org/icu4x/pull/8143.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/unicode-org/icu4x/pull/8143.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/unicode-org/icu4x/issues/8143","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/unicode-org/icu4x/pulls/8143/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/unicode-org/icu4x/pulls/8143/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/unicode-org/icu4x/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/unicode-org/icu4x/issues/8143/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/unicode-org/icu4x/statuses/7a5fdbc4c0fb7bc7c60faa94b50ac2d87eea98b7","number":8143,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Optimize segmenter result cache consumption","user":{"login":"Xuanwo","id":5351546,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzNTE1NDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5351546?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xuanwo","html_url":"https://github.com/Xuanwo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xuanwo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xuanwo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xuanwo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xuanwo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xuanwo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xuanwo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xuanwo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xuanwo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xuanwo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This PR removes the repeated allocation performed when the v1 complex-break cache consumes a boundary.\n\n## Design\n\nComplex-run-relative offsets are converted once into distances between adjacent breaks. The cache keeps natural order in `vec::IntoIter<usize>`: `as_slice().first()` peeks at the next distance and `next()` consumes it in O(1).\n\nThis follows the v2/neo cache representation and addresses the review feedback directly: there is no reversed vector, `Vec + index` state, or per-boundary offset compensation. Public API and segmentation behavior are unchanged.\n\n## Performance\n\nMeasured on an Apple M4 Max, comparing `main@3f2215305` with `PR@7a5fdbc4c`.\n\n| 1M-character full traversal | main | PR |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Word dictionary, continuous Han | 19.063 s | 31.859 ms (598x) |\n| Line dictionary, continuous Thai | 6.576 s | 22.834 ms (288x) |\n\nAt 1M characters, allocation calls and cumulative requested bytes drop from `524,325 / 1.10 TB` to `38 / 16.8 MB` for word/Han, and from `299,630 / 359 GB` to `38 / 16.8 MB` for line/Thai. Stopping after 10 boundaries remains neutral.\n\nThe merged PR #8141 workloads show the same direction on cache-heavy paths:\n\n- Thai line: LSTM `-5.4%`, dictionary `-7.1%`\n- Japanese/Han word: auto neutral, dictionary `-15.0%`\n- Mixed: line LSTM `-8.5%`, line dictionary `-2.4%`, word dictionary `-10.8%`\n\nMixed word auto is about `+4%` in the latest paired rerun; it is a small non-dictionary workload and remains the observed residual regression.\n\n```sh\nICU4X_SEGMENTER_BENCH_LARGE=1 cargo bench -p icu_segmenter --bench bench -- \"Complex Break Cache\" --noplot\n```\n\nValidation: `cargo test -p icu_segmenter --features unstable` and Clippy with `-D warnings` pass.\n\n## Changelog (N/A)\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-06-26T08:29:51Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T20:57:50Z","closed_at":"2026-08-27T10:22:35Z","merged_at":"2026-08-27T10:22:35Z","merge_commit_sha":"fb5e25f59bb1addb8da87d592ecb810923383257","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"aethanyc","id":102858,"node_id":